      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A simple, oblique osteotomy at the distal third of the metatarsal shaft is described. It is a method of relieving the pain of prolapsed metatarsal heads incarcerated in the sole and often adherent to plantar skin. The procedure has a high success rate and has stood the test of time (over a quarter of a century)."},
